From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 21:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Makefile: install the dynamic linker before libc again

The top level carries an ordering rule so that ld.so is in place before
libc.so is replaced:

  # Make sure that the dynamic linker is installed before libc.
  $(inst_slibdir)/libc-$(version).so: elf/ldso_install

but libc has been installed as libc.so$(libc.so-version) since commit
8208be389bce ("Install shared objects under their ABI names").  Nothing
builds or installs libc-$(version).so any more, so the rule names a
target that never runs and elf/ldso_install is never pulled in.  It is
the only reference to that name left in the build system.

The prerequisites of 'install' are therefore evaluated with no edge
between the top level's own $(inst_slibdir)/libc.so$(libc.so-version)
and elf/subdir_install, which installs the loader.  Because Makerules
is included before the 'install: subdir_install' line, libc is in fact
installed first, leaving a window where the new libc.so is paired with
the old ld.so.

That window became fatal in 2.44: commit a5ec880f808e ("Consolidate
pointer guard to use a relro variable instead of the TCB") makes
libc.so on i386, x86_64, powerpc, s390, sparc and sh reference
__pointer_chk_guard, which only a matching ld.so defines.  Installing
2.44 over an older glibc that programs are actively running against
kills every process started in that window:

  make: symbol lookup error: .../lib/libc.so.6: undefined symbol:
  __pointer_chk_guard, version GLIBC_PRIVATE

Point the ordering rule at the name libc is actually installed under.
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -95,8 +95,15 @@
 # Explicit dependency so that `make install-headers' works
 install-headers: install-headers-nosubdir
 
-# Make sure that the dynamic linker is installed before libc.
-$(inst_slibdir)/libc-$(version).so: elf/ldso_install
+# Make sure that the dynamic linker is installed before libc.  libc is
+# installed under its ABI name since commit 8208be389bce ("Install shared
+# objects under their ABI names"), so naming the old libc-$(version).so
+# here orders nothing: that file is never an install target.
+ifdef libc.so-version
+$(inst_slibdir)/libc.so$(libc.so-version): elf/ldso_install
+else
+$(inst_slibdir)/libc.so: elf/ldso_install
+endif
 
 .PHONY: elf/ldso_install
 elf/ldso_install:
